	  The publishable client key. Safe to embed: it authorises the client, and every row is still
	  scoped by row-level security and by the backend's own verification of the token's signature.
	  The *service* key must never appear here.

	  The URL is filled in because it is not a secret — it is the same issuer the backend verifies
	  against (`OIDC_ISSUER`) and it is public in the project's JWKS endpoint. The key is the half
	  that has to come from the Supabase dashboard, and until both are present
	  `CloudConfiguration.canSignInWithPassword` is false and the app offers the paste-a-token path
	  instead. See `docs/backend/protocol.md` and the ShareSheet.
